On-Page Architecture and Existing Blog Audit
Your dedicated game landing pages have a solid on-page foundation. For example, /games/tambola cleanly separates the informational landing page from the playable canvas (/play/tambola), contains approximately 980–1,000 words, uses descriptive H1/H2/H3 headings (About Tambola, How to play Tambola, Tips & strategy, Features, Achievements to unlock, Tambola FAQ), and carries a keyword-aligned title (Tambola Online: Play Housie with Friends Free - Game8Arena). However, site-wide internal linking is inconsistent across templates: the /blogs footer drops Tambola, Stickman Fight, and Multiverse Fighter, while the /contact and /privacy footers truncate to just 10 games (Arrow Escape through Sudoku). That leaves several high-potential games with weaker internal link equity than older puzzle titles.   

Across /blogs, 85 recent posts dated November 20–26, 2026 sit alongside earlier guides and news from November 17–19, 2026. Inspecting all 85 recent posts reveals a sharp imbalance in search potential. Sixty-seven of those 85 articles focus on Game8Arena's specific titles, and most target narrow internal features or single levels—such as Arrow Escape Level 28, Find God Discard or Search, Box Escape Mobile Controls, Color Connect Move Limit, and Blocky Blitz Hold Slot—that carry little to no search volume for a new domain. Another 13 articles in the 85-post feed (plus earlier November posts) cover unrelated AAA gaming and esports news such as GTA 6 First-Day Sales, Marvel Rivals Season 11, PUBG Mobile Bentley Collaboration, Worlds 2026, Steam Machine Price, and Splatoon 3 Update; as SEOptimer notes, trending news queries are heavily dominated by major publishers with short traffic windows, and off-topic news dilutes Game8Arena's topical authority around browser puzzles. Five more articles (Cosmic Arena Brawler Game Concept, City Defense Browser Game Concept, and three similar sketches) describe fictional games that do not exist on your site. Only the remaining evergreen genre and strategy hubs—such as Best Free Games Like 2048, Free Games to Play When Bored, How to Play Mastermind, 10 Sudoku Strategies, Undercover Word Party Game, and Tambola game options—align with organic search discovery.   

Calibrating Your Benchmark: Tambola Game Options
Your screenshot establishes a concrete baseline in your Indian Rupee (₹) keyword tool: tambola game options delivers 12.1k monthly searches, ₹0 CPC (meaning paid real-money gambling platforms are not bidding up the SERP), and a Keyword Difficulty of 19 (falling inside Similarweb's "Easy" 1–20 band). Examining live Google search results for tambola game options shows why the difficulty is low—and why your existing blog post at /blogs/tambola-game-options (published November 26, 2026) is currently mismatched to what users want.   

On Google today, the top results for tambola game options are not high-authority gaming portals. Instead, they include a five-year-old YouTube video (@SimpleTechSKS), a personal site (ashmeetsehgal.com), two scribd.com documents (Thambola-Variations and Tambola-games-docx), WikiHow, and Indian party/lifestyle blogs (partytambola.in, methri.com, wordsmithkaur.com). Experienced SEO practitioners routinely treat SERPs populated by YouTube, Scribd, forums, and personal blogs as reliable indicators of low-difficulty topics.   

Crucially, searchers typing tambola game options are hosting family nights, Diwali gatherings, birthdays, or kitty parties and want creative winning patterns ("dividends") and themed variations—such as the 36+ classic combinations (Early Five / Jaldi 5, Top/Middle/Bottom Line, Four Corners, Pyramid, Star, Plus, Cross, Zig Zag, Breakfast/Lunch/Dinner columns, Temperature, Odd/Even, Unlucky 1) and themed twists (Bollywood Dialogue, Musical, Couple/Pair, Reverse Tambola). By contrast, Game8Arena's existing /blogs/tambola-game-options page covers "Choose between solo levels and a room with friends, then learn how tickets, hints and prize claims work". Rewriting /blogs/tambola-game-options into a comprehensive winning-pattern and kitty-party variations guide—with clear links to /games/tambola and /play/tambola—aligns your existing URL directly with that 12.1k search intent.   

